  "query_preview": "..\n\nToday through tonight: Early morning fog across Sheridan county \nhas burnt off as of 10AM. For tonight, most models pull the \nsurface trough back southwest as a back door front. Behind this \nfront will be lingering low stratus clouds and fog. What little \nis left of the CAMs after losing the NAM and ARW breaks into two \ncamps with one (RRFS) showing just low stratus drifting across \nand becoming FOG on just the high terrain while the second camp \n(HRRR/RAP) show FOG moving all the way down to the low terrain and\nsocking in many locations. With no more NAM/ARW, which were the \nbest for this situation, had to tie break and split the difference\nwith fog reaching KOLF and KSDY but not Glasgow. This could \neasily change in future updates into the evening hours. With \nmassive uncertainty here and no physics packages to ensemble for a\nbetter solution, will be keeping eyes on observations up to the \nlast minute for the best solution. \n\nThursday afternoon to Monday: Above normal temps of 10 to 15 \ndegrees remain across the region though the weekend as a ridge \nplops itself over the front range and sits for a long period. \nConditions should remain dry as well.\n\nTuesday onward: Model ensembles break apart here with the GEFS \ndragging the ridge out east and replacing it with a trough, while \nEC grouping remaining in place or washes the ridge out slowly. Low\nconfidence from here onward. \n\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\n\n- Had to step in and add fog across the northeastern half of the\n  CWA as the NBM/GLAMP was not putting in anything while remaining\n  CAMs had disagreements for fog placement. \n \nHigh Confidence through Sunday for most of the forecast.\n\nLow Confidence in fog placement tonight.\n\nModerate confidence Sunday night to Monday night.\n\nLow confidence from Tuesday onward. \n\nGAH",
